    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1218">

                <pb facs="1211" n="925" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg925"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.142/1410</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Philip</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-02-13T10:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 13, 1916, 10 a. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received February 25, 8.15 a.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1570. Your 1840, February 10, 5 p. m. Turkish Government has specifically refused
                    permission for <hi rendition="#italic">Des Moines</hi> visit Beirut. Consul
                    General has telegraphed requesting Embassy instruct Blakeley not to go there.
                    Blakeley requested remain Alexandria.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Philip</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
